/* Out for review with nothing outstanding, and somebody actually asked to read it: pushed,
   proposed, handed over, nothing more to do from here for now. Every other row on this page
   is a claim on his attention and this one is not, so it should not read at the same weight.
   The green is not a severity — the rungs are still unranked against each other and still
   uncoloured. It marks the one binary this page can honestly assert: whether the next move
   is his.

   The whole row recedes, not just its name. Muting the name alone left the row reading at
   full strength anyway, because the loudest thing in it is the accent-blue ticket link and
   that was untouched — so the ticket, the age and the park control all drop back with it,
   and the state is the only thing that keeps a colour. Hover or open restores it in full:
   this is de-emphasis, not concealment, and it is still open, dated, linked and countable.
   The green edge sits on the row rather than on its summary so it stays at full strength
   through the fade, and runs the height of the disclosure when the row is opened. */
.ws[data-stage="in-review"]{box-shadow:inset 3px 0 0 var(--calm)}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"]>summary{opacity:.72}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"]>summary:hover,
.ws[data-stage="in-review"][open]>summary{opacity:1}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"] .tkt{color:var(--ink-faint)}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"] .nm{color:var(--ink-faint)}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"] .st{color:var(--calm)}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"] .park{opacity:.45}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"]>summary:hover .tkt{color:var(--accent)}
.ws[data-stage="in-review"]>summary:hover .park{opacity:1}
/* And its opposite, which is what wearing that green undeservedly was hiding: a merge
   request with nobody on it. Left neutral like every other rung — the words say it. */
.ws[data-stage="no-reviewer"]>summary{box-shadow:inset 3px 0 0 var(--hairline)}
.ws .body{padding:.2rem .7rem 1rem 7.2rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.6rem}
